Here is an example of a PHP function that sorts an array in ascending order using the bubble sort algorithm, while handling duplicate elements:

```php
function bubbleSort($arr) {
    $n = count($arr);

    // Traverse through all array elements
    for ($i = 0; $i < $n-1; $i++) {

        // Last i elements are already in place
        for ($j = 0; $j < $n-$i-1; $j++) {

            // Swap if the current element is greater than the next element
            if ($arr[$j] > $arr[$j+1]) {
                $temp = $arr[$j];
                $arr[$j] = $arr[$j+1];
                $arr[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }

    return $arr;
}

// Usage example
$myArray = [5, 8, 2, 10, 2, 1];
$sortedArray = bubbleSort($myArray);
print_r($sortedArray);
```

